{"highest":2,"ids":{"scope lens, medium: The unit probe of `_ccgl_read_holder` hand-writes the `run-status-comment.txt` fixture instead of calling `rsc_render_header` to generate it, violating CLAUDE.md's rule that data another part of the engine writes must be made with the writer's own code, never by hand. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/tests/claim-coordinator-unit-test.sh: \"cat > \"$ZBUILD_CLAIM_STORE/$_dscla4_issue/run-status-comment.txt\" <<'RSCEOF' <!-- zbuild-run-status run_id=holder-run-99 --> <!-- zbuild-holder: run-holder-99 on machine-other --> run is in progress... RSCEOF\"; happens when: When `rsc_render_header` changes the exact text of the `<!-- zbuild-holder: ... -->` comment (for example adds surrounding whitespace, renames the attribute, or changes the delimiter), `_ccgl_read_holder`'s regex silently stops matching live GitHub comments while this test continues to pass against its frozen hand-written fixture — the two diverge without any test catching it.; fix: test; ACCEPTED IF: The run-status-comment fixture used in this holder-read unit probe is generated by calling `rsc_render_header` with a known `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_HOLDER` value, so any change to the writer's format is immediately reflected in the test's Given condition and the test cannot silently pass while the reader is broken.)":"RLSCOPE-1","scope lens, low: The manifest description still names `claimed:<machine>` and the TOCTOU backoff-and-reverify behaviour that was removed from plugin.sh, leaving the manifest inconsistent with the plugin it describes. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/manifest.yaml: \"Uses GitHub issue labels   (`claimed:<machine>`) as the cross-machine claim mechanism, ported from   legacy-DoNotUse/scripts/lib/daemon-state.sh:602-720.   Has a documented TOCTOU window between add-label and re-verify. Mitigated   by random backoff (300–1100 ms) and a re-read step that drops the claim   if multiple `claimed:*` labels are observed.\"; happens when: Anyone reading manifest.yaml to understand the plugin sees a description that names a label format (`claimed:<machine>`) that no longer exists and a backoff mechanism (the `sleep` and re-verify phase) that was deleted from plugin.sh in this change.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: The manifest description reflects the single shared `zbuild:claimed` label and no longer references `claimed:<machine>` or the removed TOCTOU backoff-and-reverify behaviour.)":"RLSCOPE-2"}}
